<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Understanding X.509 and CSR Workflows</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This series uses Microsoft's&nbsp;<strong>new</strong>&nbsp;certificate management (preview) that enables devices to receive X.509 certificates automatically during provisioning. This post provides a high-level overview and points you to resources for implementation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>🆕 Preview Feature:</strong>&nbsp;Microsoft-backed X.509 certificate management was announced in November 2025 and is currently in public preview.&nbsp;</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Not recommended for production workloads.</strong>&nbsp;For details, see&nbsp;<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/iot-hub/iot-hub-certificate-management-overview">Certificate Management Overview</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {"textColor":"#f6f6f4"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-f-6-f-6-f-4-color has-text-color">Contents:</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true,"textColor":"#f6f6f4"} -->
<ol class="wp-block-list has-f-6-f-6-f-4-color has-text-color"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://www.petecodes.co.uk/iot-hub-with-adr-and-certificate-management-part-1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Introduction</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://www.petecodes.co.uk/iot-hub-with-adr-and-certificate-management-part-2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">A DPS Primer</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://www.petecodes.co.uk/iot-hub-with-adr-and-certificate-management-part-3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Creating DPS, IoT Hub and ADR Instances</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://www.petecodes.co.uk/iot-hub-with-adr-and-certificate-management-part-4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Understanding X.509 and CSR Workflows</a> (This Post)</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><a href="https://www.petecodes.co.uk/iot-hub-with-adr-and-certificate-management-part-5" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The Device Application</a></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="two-types-of-certificates">Two Types of Certificates</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The new certificate management service makes use of a&nbsp;<strong>two-phase approach</strong>:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="phase-1-onboarding-credentials">Phase 1: Onboarding Credentials</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong>&nbsp;Device authenticates to DPS during initial provisioning</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Options:</strong>&nbsp;X.509 certificates (from third-party CA), symmetric keys, or TPM</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Your responsibility:</strong>&nbsp;Pre-install on device before shipment</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Lifespan:</strong>&nbsp;Long-lived or used once for initial authentication</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="phase-2-operational-certificates-microsoft-managed">Phase 2: Operational Certificates (Microsoft-Managed)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong>&nbsp;Device authenticates to IoT Hub for ongoing operations</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>How it works:</strong>&nbsp;Automatically issued by DPS during provisioning via CSR</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Generated on:</strong>&nbsp;Device itself (private key never leaves device)</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Lifespan:</strong>&nbsp;Short-lived (1-90 days), automatically renewed</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Security:</strong>&nbsp;Higher security, no key transport</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The following diagram shows the complete provisioning flow:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:merpress/mermaidjs -->
<div class="wp-block-merpress-mermaidjs diagram-source-mermaid"><pre class="mermaid">sequenceDiagram
    participant Device as IoT Device
    participant DPS as DPS
    participant ADR as ADR
    participant PKI as PKI-R&lt;br/>(Issuing CA)
    participant Hub as IoT Hub

    Note over Device: Pre-configured with&lt;br/>onboarding credential&lt;br/>and DPS endpoint

    Note over DPS: Configure enrollment:&lt;br/>1) Define onboarding method&lt;br/>2) Link to ADR policy

    Note over ADR: Configure credential&lt;br/>(Root CA) and&lt;br/>policies (ICAs)

    Note over PKI: Manage hierarchy of&lt;br/>Certificate&lt;br/>Authorities (CAs)

    Note over Hub: Store CA and&lt;br/>validate leaf certs

    Device->>DPS: 1. Provisioning Request + CSR
    Note over Device,DPS: Device sends Certificate Signing Request

    DPS->>DPS: 2. Verify onboarding credential
    
    DPS->>Hub: 3. Provision device to Hub
    DPS->>ADR: 3. Register device in ADR
    
    Hub-->>DPS: Device created
    ADR-->>DPS: Device registered

    DPS->>PKI: 4. Request operational certificate
    Note over DPS,PKI: Forward CSR to issuing CA

    PKI->>PKI: 5. ICA signs and returns&lt;br/>operational certificate
    
    PKI-->>DPS: 6. Operational cert + chain

    DPS-->>Device: 6. Return operational cert&lt;br/>+ Hub endpoint

    Device->>Hub: 7. Authenticate with IoT Hub&lt;br/>using operational certificate chain
    
    Note over Device,Hub: Device uses newly issued&lt;br/>operational certificate for&lt;br/>all future communications
</pre></div>
<!-- /wp:merpress/mermaidjs -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Key Steps:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Device sends provisioning request + CSR</strong>&nbsp;- Device authenticates with onboarding credential and submits Certificate Signing Request</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>DPS verifies onboarding credential</strong>&nbsp;- Validates device identity (X.509, symmetric key, or TPM)</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Device provisioned to Hub and registered in ADR</strong>&nbsp;- Device identity created in both services</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Request operational certificate</strong>&nbsp;- DPS uses the CSR to request an operational certificate from the PKI. The PKI validates the CSR and forwards it to the policy (issuing CA) linked to the DPS enrollment.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>ICA signs and returns operational certificate</strong>&nbsp;- Issuing CA issues leaf certificate</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Return operational cert + Hub endpoint</strong>&nbsp;- DPS sends certificate chain back to device</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Device authenticates with IoT Hub</strong>&nbsp;- Device uses new operational certificate for all future connections</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="microsoft-managed-pki-architecture">Microsoft-Managed PKI Architecture</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Azure Device Registry (ADR) manages a dedicated PKI for your namespace:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Root CA (Credential):</strong>&nbsp;One unique root CA per ADR namespace, managed by Microsoft using Azure Managed HSM</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Issuing CA (Policy):</strong>&nbsp;One issuing CA per policy, defines certificate validity (1-90 days)</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Leaf Certificate (Operational):</strong>&nbsp;End-entity certificate issued to device by issuing CA</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The issuing CA certificates are automatically synced from ADR to all linked IoT Hubs, enabling Hub to authenticate devices.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="key-features">Key Features</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:table -->
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table class="has-fixed-layout"><thead><tr><th class="has-text-align-left" data-align="left">Feature</th><th class="has-text-align-left" data-align="left">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Algorithms</strong></td><td>ECC (ECDSA) with NIST P-384 curve, SHA-384 hashing</td></tr><tr><td><strong>HSM Keys</strong></td><td>Azure Managed HSM (no additional subscription required)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Certificate Validity</strong></td><td>1-90 days (configurable per policy)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Protocols</strong></td><td>HTTP and MQTT during provisioning</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Renewal</strong></td><td>Device-initiated via DPS registration call</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CA Sync</strong></td><td>Automatic sync from ADR to linked IoT Hubs</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<!-- /wp:table -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="what-you-need-to-do">What You'll Be Doing</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For this series, you'll create&nbsp;<strong>onboarding credentials</strong>&nbsp;(Phase 1) - we provide automation scripts:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Preview Reminder:</strong>&nbsp;Microsoft-backed X.509 certificate management is&nbsp;<strong>new and in public preview</strong>. Operational certificates (Phase 2) are issued by ADR during provisioning and are&nbsp;<strong>not recommended for production workloads</strong>&nbsp;during preview.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="quick-setup-automated-x509-bootstrap-certificates-if-you-didnt-already-run-the-full-setup-script">Quick Setup: Automated X.509 Bootstrap Certificates (if you didn't already run the full setup script!)</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

